            "id": "SK35VZEHV3QC5FZ",
            "title": "3D Contactless Mouse (Interactive 3D Position Sensor)",
            "body": "<p>Recently, I have made this 3D contactless mouse, which I use to control (or to try to control) my computer cursor. You can see the functionalities in the video below :<\/p><iframe allowfullscreen=\"true\" class=\"ql-video\" data-wat-video-found=\"true\" frameborder=\"0\" height=\"360\" id=\"waf_detected_youtube0\" src=\"//www.youtube.com/embed/pj1e4YbxBwM?rel=0&amp;enablejsapi=1&amp;origin=https://www.instructables.com&amp;enablejsapi=1&amp;origin=https://www.instructables.com\" width=\"640\"><\/iframe><p>All the computation is made on the arduino leonardo, which emulates a mouse. In fact, it's a very simple vision system that uses only five ultrasonic range sensors to make converge the robot towards the object and to lock its orientation on it by the primitive detection of the edges I've developped.<\/p><p>In this Instructable, I will show you how to build your own version of this amazing device!<\/p>",
            "url": "https://www.instructables.com/3D-Contactless-Mouse-Interactive-3D-Position-Senso/"
        },
