            "showUrl": "/3D-Contactless-Mouse-Interactive-3D-Position-Senso/step1/List-of-Materials/",
            "id": "SDPU287HV3QC62G",
            "title": "List of Materials",
            "body": "<ol><li data-list=\"bullet\">The 3D printed parts listed below<\/li><li data-list=\"bullet\">A small screw and two bolts (I can't tell the type but the screw is about 1/8'' in diameter, 1'' in lenght)<\/li><li data-list=\"bullet\">A rotationnal bearing (I've made one with a small rod and a small roller taken in a cassette player)<\/li><li data-list=\"bullet\">Some counterweight (I use three 25 cents)<\/li><li data-list=\"bullet\">An Arduino Leonardo<\/li><li data-list=\"bullet\">Six micro servomotors 9g<\/li><li data-list=\"bullet\">Five ultrasonic range finder<\/li><li data-list=\"bullet\">A lot of connecting wires (15 female to male and 18 male to male, plus some breadboard wire)<\/li><li data-list=\"bullet\">A micro usb to usb A wire<\/li><li data-list=\"bullet\">An arduino protoshield with a mini breadboard<\/li><li data-list=\"bullet\">An external 5V DC power supply for the servos<\/li><li data-list=\"bullet\">A 555 timer<\/li><li data-list=\"bullet\">A LM386 amplifier<\/li><li data-list=\"bullet\">An electret microphone<\/li><li data-list=\"bullet\">Resistances (2X 4.7kΩ, 1X 10kΩ, 1X 100kΩ)<\/li><li data-list=\"bullet\">Capacitors (3X 10nF, 1X 1µF)<\/li><\/ol><p>Tools :<\/p><ol><li data-list=\"bullet\">A glue gun<\/li><li data-list=\"bullet\">A computer<\/li><\/ol>",
            "url": "https://www.instructables.com/3D-Contactless-Mouse-Interactive-3D-Position-Senso/step1/List-of-Materials/"
        },
